-- Rifts World Book 19: Australia, batch 3: vehicles and power armor.
-- Nine rows with their M.D.C.-by-location tables and weapon lists: three
-- suits of power armor (the Mokoloi Prey-Stalker, printed 145-148; the Modular
-- Powered Armor "Rusty", 210-212; the X50 "Bushbasher", 212-214) and the six
-- Notable Vehicles (printed 214-223). 80 location rows, 35 weapon rows.
-- book-reconcile checked every figure; it found three main-body location rows
-- missing and one wrong remark, both corrected here.
-- See apps/character-creator/docs/surveys/australia.md.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/add-australia-vehicles.sql
--
-- READ IN COLUMN ORDER (scripts/read-columns.py) and off renders where a
-- block was scrambled, then checked again by book-reconcile: these pages set
-- each stat block beside line art and the plain text layer interleaves the
-- columns.
--
-- THE PREY-STALKER ROW IS INCOMPLETE, AND SAYS SO. The source PDF binds
-- printed page 145 twice and has no page 146. That page holds the first four
-- weapon entries, the head of the Sonic Blast entry, and the suit's speed,
-- size, weight and price. None of it is stored or guessed. The book prints
-- two headings for this suit (the narrative and the stat block); it is one
-- row.
--
-- CONVENTIONS:
--   cost is the lowest printed price; the others are in cost_note. The
--     Crawler's is the stripped Outback sale, the Viper's the fuel-powered
--     model, the Stinger's the model without the VR interface.
--   A printed range stores its low end: the Fliers' main body (200 to 300)
--     and weight (5-12 tons).
--   weight_tons is converted from pounds for the two City power armors and
--     the Stinger; the printed weight is in the description.
--   The Slicer's mini-torpedo launcher prints no M.D.C.: NULL.
--   A weapon the book lists with no damage figure of its own (optics, the
--     Rusty's forearm weapons by page reference) is in the description, not a
--     weapon row.
--
-- Pure ASCII, LF. Re-running it is a no-op.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles
  (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, cost, cost_note, description, source_book)
VALUES
  ('mokoloi-prey-stalker-power-armor', 'Mokoloi "Prey-Stalker" Techno-Wizard Power Armor', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One Mokoloi', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 280, NULL, 'Not read: Printed page 146 is missing from the source PDF (page 145 is bound in twice).', 'Techno-Wizard Prey-Stalker Power Armor; Purpose: Assault, Anti-Personnel. Mokoloi (Croc-men) Techno-Wizard armor; heavy M.D.C. protection and weapons, does not boost attributes. Supernatural P.S. 30. Withstands depth of one mile (1.6 km), double normal swimming speed, breathes underwater 2 hours at a time without visible air supply. Levitate, Float in Air, Repel Animals as 4th level spells, each 6 times per 24 hours. Regenerates 2D6+6 M.D.C. per 24 hours. Nightvision 600 ft, see invisible, sense magic (5th level). Creation: initial P.P.E. 325; spells Constrain Being (20), Energy Field (10), Armor of Ithan (10), Invisible Armor (30), Power Weapon (35), Swim as a Fish superior (12), Breathe Without Air (5), Float in Air (5), levitation (5), Superhuman Speed (10), Superhuman Strength (10), Mend the Broken (10+), Shockwave (35), Fire Ball (10), Electric Arc (8), Fireblast (8), Globe of Daylight (2), See the Invisible (4), Nightvision (6), Sense Magic (4) plus secret incantations. Materials: mechanical components, armor plating, silver plating for blades/claws/mechanics, two large rose quartz crystals for eyes, a Tectonic Entity or energy sphere locked inside as power source (content with its role), secret components. Build time 960 to 1100 hours (about 4-8 months). INCOMPLETE ROW. Printed page 146 is missing from the source PDF (page 145 is bound in twice). That page holds weapon items 1-4 (the laser eyes, back flame gun, lava spit and the arm and tail blades), the head of the Sonic Blast entry with its damage, and the speed, size, weight and price of the suit. Those are not stored; the weapons below are the ones the surviving pages print, the Sonic Blast without its damage. The suits sensors give +1 to strike and +1 to dodge with long-range weaponry only.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.145-148'),
  ('apaa-rusty-modular-power-armor', 'Modular Powered Armor "Rusty" (APAA)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One', NULL, 'Running: 55 mph (88 km) maximum, 30% of usual fatigue rate; can be souped up to 70 mph (112 km) for an additional 30,000 dollars/credits. Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or 20 feet (6.1 m) across', 'Not possible without a jet pack; standard jet pack max altitude 2000 feet (610 m), speed 120 mph (192 km)', 'Swim 5 mph (4.3 knots/8 km) for an hour at a time; underwater jet pack 20 mph (17.2 knots/32 km) indefinitely; pressure to 1200 feet (366 m)', 'Height: 8 feet (2.4 m) tall. Width: From 3 feet (0.9 m). Length: 3 feet (0.9 m); varies slightly with the different backpacks and attachments', 0.26, 200, 1700000, 'Market Cost: 1.7 to 2 million in the Outback. Each Weapon System is an extra cost.', 'Official Designation: Assault Power Armor Alpha (APAA); Common Name: Rusty; Purpose: Multi-Purpose/General Purpose. Light modular environmental power armor, depth 1200 ft. P.S. equal to 28. Cargo: snap-on hard case backpack plus torso compartment (handgun, four extra clips, knife, hand-held radio) and holster belt with six pouches. Nuclear power, average life 20 years. Sensors: full optical systems, telescopic vision, passive nightvision, thermo-imaging, infrared. Extra armor: main body +50% (100 M.D.C.), other parts +20%, $800 per M.D.C. point; City Military suits 260-300 main body, Outback-sold basic suits start at 200. Attachments (jet pack, underwater pack, hook and winch, flame thrower with fuel tank, sensor packs, long-range radio/radar) typically $15,000-$30,000 each. Bugged: Cities can track the wearer and silent alarms trigger if used against a City or Military Outpost; -45% for Engineer or Cyber-Specter to find and deactivate (printed in intro text). Traded suits are usually stripped to one or two weapon systems. Weight as printed: 520 pounds (235 kg).', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.210-212'),
  ('x50-bushbasher-power-armor', 'X50 "Bushbasher" Power Armor (APAB)', 'rifts', 'power-armor', 'One', NULL, 'Running: 35 mph (56 km) maximum, 20% of usual fatigue rate. Leaping: 5 feet (1.5 m) high or 10 feet (3 m) across', 'Not possible without a jet pack', 'Swim 5 mph (4.3 knots/8 km) for an hour at a time; underwater jet pack 20 mph (17.2 knots/32 km) indefinitely; pressure to 1200 feet (366 m)', 'Height: 7 feet (2.1 m); 8 feet (2.4 m) with part of the shoulder gun protruding when stored on the shoulder pointing up. Width: 3 feet (.9m). Length: 3 feet (.9 m); may vary with backpack attachments', 0.35, 240, 2800000, 'Black Market Cost: City cost is 2.8 million for a new suit of power armor fully loaded with weapon systems. Outback: rare stripped-down versions (no weapons other than Vibro-Blades, 20% less armor) sell for three times that; fully loaded versions (illegal) sell for 10 times the base price.', 'Official Designation: Assault Power Armor Beta (APAB); Common Name: Bushbasher; Primary Purpose: Infantry Assault and Espionage. Environmental power armor, depth 1200 ft; Melbourne/Perth Military standard for about 40 years. P.S. equal to 30. Nuclear power, average life 20 years. Sensors: full optical systems, telescopic vision, passive nightvision, thermo-imaging, infrared. Field troops typically carry four smoke and six fragmentation grenades. Jet pack and underwater pack attach to back. Outback-traded suits typically have one weapon system (usually Vibro-Blades) and 20% less M.D.C. Bugged for City tracking (printed in the Rusty intro text). No cargo line printed. Weight as printed: 700 pounds (315 kg).', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.212-214'),
  ('nt-1200-devil-4x4', '"Devil" 4x4 NT-1200 Multi-Purpose Vehicle', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Three: a driver, gunner, and communications officer', 'Five more seated comfortably on bench seats, seven cramped; six others can ride on the exterior hand-holds in an emergency if speed is held under 35 mph (56 km)', 'Cruising: 45 mph (72 km); Maximum Speed: 140 mph (224 km); Maximum Off-Road Speed: 110 mph (176 km)', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 6 feet (1.8 m), sensor cluster adds 3 feet (0.9 m) for overall 9 feet (2.7 m). Width: 7 feet (2.1 m) body alone, 11 feet (3.3 m) overall. Length: 18 feet (5.5 m)', 8.5, 225, 180000, '$180,000 for a new, undamaged civilian vehicle (30% less armor, no weapons). Military units with standard weaponry and sensors $490,000. Price may vary 10-30% up or down; usually up. Component costs: grenade launcher $42,000, rail gun $130,000, comms suite $30,000, sensors $120,000, other onboard systems $60,000; two extra weapon systems for under $200,000.', 'NT-1200 Multi-Purpose Vehicle (stat block titled "Devil 4x4 Vehicle"). All-terrain jeep-style small squad transport and light combat vehicle; independent suspension, four wheel drive. Military version: pop-up grenade launcher, bonnet rail gun or laser, comms suite (200 mi/320 km), sensors (20 mile/32 km radar, targeting computer +1 to strike with onboard weapons), self-destruct feature. All models: air conditioning, 4 hour oxygen supply, small fridge, 3 gallons water, first-aid kit, A/V display, CD player, crash air bags (half damage to passengers). Range 300 miles (480 km) combustion, unlimited nuclear; about 36% have solar collector and battery adding 120 miles (192 km). Rear cargo compartment 6 ft wide x 3 ft long x 4 ft deep (6 ft long with rear seats folded); carries 5 tons, tows 12 tons, speed -30% when hauling over 6 tons. Civilian model has 30% less M.D.C. and no weapons. Military models can add two more weapon systems. Weight as printed: 8.5 tons.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.214-215'),
  ('nt-6000-crawler-apc', '"Crawler" APC NT-6000 All-Terrain Half-Track', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Four: a driver, communications engineer/navigator, gunner and soldier escort/defender', 'Up to four additional personnel in the four-door front cab; the rear holds a platoon of 40 troops in body armor, or 26 in power armor', 'Cruising: 35-50 mph (56 to 80 km); Maximum Speed: 100 mph (160 km); Maximum Off-Road Speed: 80 mph (128 km)', NULL, NULL, 'Height: 8 feet, 8 inches (2.65 m) main body; weapons and sensor/communications cluster add 4 feet (1.2 m) for overall 12 feet, 8 inches (roughly 3.9 m). Width: 9 feet, 4 inches (2.8 m). Length: 28 feet (8.5 m)', 18, 440, 514000, '$940,000 for a standard Military vehicle. Occasionally sold or traded to an Outback community minus all weaponry and sensors, less 40% of the M.D.C., with a fuel-solar system (never nuclear), at $514,000; may sell for twice that on the secondary market. Component costs: mini-missile launcher $140,000 plus $5000 per missile; main gun approx. $160,000; comms $30,000; sensors $120,000; other onboard systems $60,000; additional weapons average around $150,000 each.', 'NT-6000 All-Terrain Half-Track (stat block titled "Crawler Half-track"). Armored personnel carrier and cargo hauler. Front two wheels solid rubber, rear on tank tracks; ramp slides out of cargo bay. Roughly half nuclear (effectively unlimited range, 20 year life), half combustion (500 mile/804 km) with solar/electric battery adding 120 miles (192 km). Trailer section carries up to 100 tons and pulls 200 tons more, speed -30%. Military models have the same comms suite (200 mi/320 km), sensors (20 mile radar, targeting computer +1 to strike) and onboard systems as the Devil, and can take two additional weapon systems. Weight as printed: 18 tons.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.215-217'),
  ('slicer-patrol-boat', '"Slicer" Patrol Boat', 'rifts', 'ship', '9-13: captain/pilot, helmsman/co-pilot, navigator/communications officer, two gunners, 2-4 sailors/Marines/combat troops and 2-4 Power Armor troops', '6-10 additional personnel on the bridge; the belly holds up to 10 more fully armed Marines', NULL, NULL, 'Cruising: 40 mph (64 km/34 knots); Maximum Speed: 140 mph (224 km/123 knots)', 'Height: 6 feet (1.8 m) from water level to top of cabin, 12 feet (3.7 m) with sensor mast; draft of 4 feet 4 inches (1.3 m) below water. Width: 11 feet (3.4 m). Length: 44 feet (13.4 m)', 12.5, 500, 1600000, '1.6 million for a nuclear powered vessel with all weaponry and sensors. Not available on the open market except via the black market; very rare.', 'Slicer Patrol Boat; Purpose: Fast Response Patrol Boat (no NT designation printed). Bonus: +2 to dodge. About one third combustion (600 miles/960 km), two thirds nuclear with unlimited range (20 year life). Supplies for the skeleton crew of 4 for 3 months (1 month with soldier unit). Hold carries 6 tons and tows 40 tons; speed -60% when hauling over 10 tons. Comms 500 miles (800 km); long (30 mi/48 km) and short (2 mi/3.2 km) radar tracking up to 36 targets; passive sonar 1 mile (1.6 km). Air conditioning with 6 hour oxygen supply, basic medical equipment, A/V, four inflatable rafts (6 men each, 3 days supplies, A.R. 8, 50 S.D.C.). Sensor mast destroyed: other sensors at -40%. Flying bridge destroyed: use bow bridge with no penalty (below-decks -20% to detect ambushes). Main cabin destroyed: speed -20%. Standard crew includes Trencher Power Armor troops. Weight as printed: 12.5 tons.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.217-218'),
  ('nt-v40-viper-attack-chopper', '"Viper" NT-V40 Multi-Purpose Attack Chopper', 'rifts', 'vehicle', 'Two minimum, typically four: pilot, co-pilot/communications, and two door gunners', 'Four can ride comfortably in the rear compartment with the door gunners; six cramped', 'Not possible unless hauled by another vehicle', 'Can hover stationary or achieve a maximum of 480 mph (768 km); maximum altitude 5000 feet (1524 m)', NULL, 'Height: 8 feet (2.4 m) for body, 14 feet (4.3 m) including rotor blades. Width: 10 feet (3 m) wing tip to wing tip with rotors folded, or 35 feet (10.7 m) with rotors deployed. Length: 38 feet (11.6 m)', 6.5, 210, 1800000, '3.9 million for a nuclear powered Viper (70%), or 1.8 for a fuel powered chopper. Super-rare outside the Tech-Cities.', 'NT-V40 Multi-Purpose Attack Chopper (stat block titled "NT-V40 Attack Chopper"). Primary purpose Air Assault, Rescue and Troop Support; secondary Reconnaissance, Insertion and Extraction. Limited stealth, can rig for silent running at reduced speed. Range 500 miles (800 km) combustion, unlimited nuclear (20 year life). Cargo up to one ton. Folding telescoping rotors stored in a compartment holding a reserve pair that deploy within about one melee action if the main rotors are destroyed (200 ft/61 m altitude lost mid-air). Ejector seats for pilot and co-pilot only. Sensors: thermographic, low light nightvision, HUD, targeting scope, laser targeting, 20 mile (32 km) radar, loudspeaker, infrared, directional spy microphone, external camera, 300 mile (480 km) comms, onboard computer; sealed filtered cockpit. May carry 1-4 jet-pack power armor troopers. Bonuses: +1 to strike with all ranged weaponry, +1 to dodge, +2 on initiative. Weight as printed: 6.5 tons. The fuel-powered price is printed as "1.8" with no "million".', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.218-220'),
  ('vr-500x-stinger', 'VR-500X "Stinger" Remote Mini-Helicopter', 'rifts', 'drone', 'Unmanned drone. If controlled by VR interface, one human operator who can be up to 50 miles (80 km) away (double in flat desert or grasslands without mountains or trees)', NULL, 'Not possible, must be hauled by another vehicle', 'May hover in place or achieve a maximum of 460 mph (736 km); maximum altitude 1800 feet (167.6 m)', NULL, 'Height: 3 feet (0.9 m). Width: 3 feet (0.9 m) wing tip to wing tip, 12 feet (3.7 m) total with rotors running. Length: 14 feet (4.3 m)', 0.5, 60, 550000, '760,000 for a new, undamaged Stinger with full arms and VR interface. Excluding the VR drops the price to 550,000.', 'VR-500X Remote Mini-Helicopter (stat block titled "VR-500X Stinger Robot"); Purpose: Defense and Patrol/Reconnaissance. Patrol drone, spotter/spy, defense. Range approx. 400 miles (640 km); power combustion or electric with approx. one hour flight/fuel time; cargo none. One VR operator can control 1-4 Stingers which then mimic the lead unit like a swarm. Three cameras; Perth model has swivelling (90 deg up/down, 360 deg) camera/sensor under the gun mount and a pair under the rotors, Melbourne model launches missiles from the underbelly and has VTOL jets in place of sensor wings. Without a VR operator it acts predictably (all bonuses halved, round down). Sensors: thermographic, low light, HUD, targeting scope, laser targeting, terrain following radar, loudspeaker, infrared, microphone, camera, 100 mile (160 km) comms. Weight as printed: 1000 pounds (450 kg). Printed oddities, stored as printed: the ceiling reads 1800 feet (167.6 m), which do not agree; the prose gives six mini-missiles per wing where the weapon entry gives 24 rockets.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.220-222'),
  ('one-and-two-man-fliers', 'One & Two Man Fliers', 'rifts', 'vehicle', '1-2; typically a pilot or pilot and co-pilot/gunner', NULL, 'Not possible unless hauled by another vehicle', 'Fliers can hover stationary or achieve a maximum of 480 mph (768 km); maximum altitude typically 5000 feet (1524 m)', NULL, 'Height: Varies from 8-12 feet (2.4 to 3.6 m). Width: Varies from 10-20 feet (3 to 6 m) depending on wingspan. Length: Varies from 12 to 22 feet (3.6 to 6.7 m)', 5, 200, 2800000, '2.8 to 6.2 million; reduce by half if not nuclear powered (approximately half are nuclear powered).', 'One & Two Man Fliers: small VTOL aircraft used exclusively by the Perth and Melbourne militaries. One combined entry; the book prints no separate one-man and two-man figures. Primary purpose Air Assault and Troop Support. Most share the same basic features, varying 10-30% in speed and in weapon combinations. VTOL, hover, low and slow flight (down to 5 feet/1.5 m above ground); not faster than the assault helicopter. Range 500 miles (800 km) combustion, unlimited nuclear (20 year life). Cargo none other than payload and crew. Ejector seats and sensors same as the Viper. Bonuses: +1 to strike with all ranged weaponry, +2 to dodge, +1 on initiative. Most two-man models can take two additional light weapons or one heavy, but only 40% have extras. Weight as printed: Varies from 5-12 tons. One combined entry: the book prints ranges, not separate one-man and two-man figures. Main body is 200 to 300 M.D.C. and weight 5-12 tons; the low ends are stored. The secondary gun range reads 1600 feet (183 m), which do not agree.', 'Rifts World Book 19: Australia p.222-223');

